    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0292" n="184" xml:id="pg184"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic"> Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Shannon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                        1893</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 167.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 295 of 10th
                    ultimo, and the draft therewith for $2,500, paid by Salvador in respect of
                    injury to consular property at San Salvador in July 1890, and to Consul H. E.
                    Myers in property and in person.</p>
                <p>As I have informed the Hon. Mr. Pickler, the Department will retain as payment
                    for the consular property the sum of $137.25 named in Mr. Myers’s letter of
                    February 4, 1891.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
